# The whole arc, from one ark to the next.
#
# **Sean, 2026-09-20**, naming what this prototype is for: *the core game loop: start with an ark ->
# develop a planet -> launch an ark.* **This is that loop and nothing else** - every other test here
# says one thing about one rule, and this one says the things join up.
#
# **What it adds is that what one rule leaves is what the next one needs.** Every piece is checked
# on its own already - and a suite of pieces can pass entire while the arc they are pieces of does
# not close, because no test of a piece ever looks at the next one.
#
# **Four turns, and what makes it four is that a built thing arrives spent.** `build-extractor`
# leaves an extractor with `working:0`, so the energy it wants cannot be mined until the turn
# restores it - which is the same shape as an ark arriving with no move.
#
# ## What each turn is for
#
# **Turn one is the landing.** The ark becomes two extractors and two citizens, and nothing else can
# happen: both extractors are spent and both citizens have no `bearing` yet. Ending the turn is the
# whole of the turn.
#
# **Turn two is food.** Two citizens make two labours; one is spent on the food extractor and the
# other is wasted, because there is nothing else worth doing with it. **The waste is the point of
# the turn**: six food feeds two citizens at `upkeep` and the four left over let `breed` fire twice,
# so the settlement is four citizens by the end of it.
#
# **Turn three is the energy extractor.** Four labours: one for food, one for metal, one to build,
# and one wasted. The six metal that `work` produced is spent down to five and then discarded at the
# turn's end, because nothing here has a bin - and none of it is needed, because turn four mines its
# own.
#
# **Turn four is the launch.** Six labours, of which three are used: metal, energy, and the launch
# itself. **The ark it leaves is spent**, `moving:0` and `gathering:0`, which is what an ark always
# is on the turn it is made.
#
# ## What the end state says
#
# **Six citizens, no food, and three labours standing.** The settlement that built the ark is still
# there and still hungry - a launch is not a departure, it is a thing built. **What happens to them
# next is the next turn's problem**, and nothing here pretends otherwise.
#
# **Nothing is stored.** Five metal and five energy lie loose and would go at the turn's end; the
# test stops before that, because what it is about is the arc rather than the housekeeping.
#
# **This test is brittle and that is correct.** Every number in it is a consequence of every rule's
# cost, so tuning any of them moves it - which is what an acceptance test for *the loop closes* is
# supposed to do.

{test name:an-ark-lands-a-planet-is-developed-and-an-ark-leaves}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{place id:1 of:territory-1 layer:surface name:place-1}
{place id:2 of:territory-1 layer:orbit name:place-2}
{capacity of:deposit for:extractor what:resource per:place} -> 1
{deposit where:place-1 what:metal density:6} -> 1
{deposit where:place-1 what:food density:6} -> 1
{deposit where:place-1 what:energy density:6} -> 1
{ark where:place-2 moving:1 gathering:1} -> 1

{when}
{deploy where:place-2}
{end-turn}
{toil where:place-1}
{work where:place-1 what:food}
{end-turn}
{toil where:place-1}
{work where:place-1 what:food}
{work where:place-1 what:metal}
{build-extractor where:place-1 what:energy}
{end-turn}
{toil where:place-1}
{work where:place-1 what:metal}
{work where:place-1 what:energy}
{launch where:place-1}

{then}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{place id:1 of:territory-1 layer:surface name:place-1}
{place id:2 of:territory-1 layer:orbit name:place-2}
{capacity of:deposit for:extractor what:resource per:place} -> 1
{deposit where:place-1 what:metal density:6} -> 1
{deposit where:place-1 what:food density:6} -> 1
{deposit where:place-1 what:energy density:6} -> 1
{extractor where:place-1 what:metal working:0} -> 1
{extractor where:place-1 what:food working:1} -> 1
{extractor where:place-1 what:energy working:0} -> 1
{citizen where:place-1 hungry:1 bearing:1 laboring:0} -> 6
{labor where:place-1} -> 3
{metal where:place-1} -> 5
{energy where:place-1} -> 5
{ark where:place-2 moving:0 gathering:0} -> 1
